<h3>Wrap-up — your own, every day, first</h3>
<p>The team problem is only solved <strong>after your own runs well every day</strong>. First get a feel for deciding <strong>how you route and where to put your data</strong> yourself. That is the first gate.</p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">In one sentence</span>
    There is one condition for a good Second Brain — <strong>"it knows where my data lives, knows in what order to look, and gives an accurate answer."</strong> Go back to the beginning and reread <a href="#!sb-intro">What is a Second Brain</a>, and you will understand why "can you find it again?" was everything.
</div>
